# Phase 2: Ingestion Service — Walkthrough

Phase 2 of **PulseStream** has been implemented, tested, and verified. The Ingestion Service ingests events concurrently from real-world Wikipedia Recent Changes and synthetic simulations, validates them against the Avro schema, and publishes them to Kafka with DLQ routing.

---

## What Was Built

### 1. Connectors (`src/ingestion/connectors/`)
- [simulator.py](file:///c:/Users/Akhil%20Anwar/projects/Personal/project/src/ingestion/connectors/simulator.py):
  - Async generator `EventSimulator.stream_events()`
  - Modes: `steady`, `burst` (10x rate spike), `chaos`, and `ramp`.
  - Zipf power-law distribution for realistic user activity and community popularity skew.
  - Chaos injection: duplicates (5%), malformed structures (2%), and out-of-order timestamps.
- [wikipedia.py](file:///c:/Users/Akhil%20Anwar/projects/Personal/project/src/ingestion/connectors/wikipedia.py):
  - SSE client consuming from `https://stream.wikimedia.org/v2/stream/recentchange`.
  - Compliant `User-Agent` header (`PulseStream/1.0`).
  - Canonical event type mapping: `edit`/`new` $\to$ `POST_CREATED`, `log` $\to$ `USER_JOINED`, `categorize` $\to$ `REACTION_ADDED`.
  - Namespace filter: main article (`0`) and user (`2`) namespaces.
  - Automatic reconnection with exponential backoff and jitter.

### 2. Pipeline (`src/ingestion/pipeline.py`)
- `IngestionPipeline`:
  - `receive` $\to$ `normalize` $\to$ `validate_avro` $\to$ `assign_id` $\to$ `publish`.
  - Valid events are Avro-serialized and produced to `pulsestream.events` using community/user partition key hashing.
  - Validation failures or malformed events are automatically routed to `pulsestream.events.dlq` with error context.
  - Metrics tracking: `ingestion_events_total` and `ingestion_events_rejected_total`.

### 3. Service Entry Point & Docker
- [src/ingestion/main.py](file:///c:/Users/Akhil%20Anwar/projects/Personal/project/src/ingestion/main.py):
  - Asynchronous task coordination running enabled connectors concurrently.
  - Prometheus metrics server on port `9100`.
  - Graceful shutdown handling (`SIGINT`/`SIGTERM`), draining pending events and flushing the Kafka producer.
- [docker/Dockerfile.ingestion](file:///c:/Users/Akhil%20Anwar/projects/Personal/project/docker/Dockerfile.ingestion) & [docker/docker-compose.yml](file:///c:/Users/Akhil%20Anwar/projects/Personal/project/docker/docker-compose.yml): Added `ingestion` container service (0.25 CPU, 256MB RAM).
- [Makefile](file:///c:/Users/Akhil%20Anwar/projects/Personal/project/Makefile): Added `ingestion` target.

